<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Batepro year earnings rise, sees growth.</title>
<headline>Batepro year earnings rise, sees growth.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ten months June 30 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     35.68	 vs    55.69</p>
<p>    Final div (cts)	 11.5	  vs    12.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   13.09	 vs     3.37</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   22.59	 vs     3.67</p>
<p>    Tax			  5.7	  vs     0.30</p>
<p>    Interest paid	    3.76	 vs     0.02</p>
<p>    Turnover		 999.85	 vs    58.15</p>
<p>Div payable: October 25</p>
<p>on register: October 11</p>
<p>Full name: Bateman Project Holdings Ltd (engineering)</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said prospects for the coming year looked encouraging and the group was budgeting for further growth.</p>
<p>The firm said the turnover figure for 1995/96 is notional and represents the value of contract work handled for clients where disbursements for the related equipment supply and construction labour are made by the client.</p>
<p>The comparative figures are for a 12 month period.</p>
<p>The firm now has 36,687,000 shares in issue compared to 6,042,000 for the comparative period.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
